MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

You need to either import those packages into your namespace or use ::

ggplot2::ggplot(result,aes(x=slope,y=..density..), environment = environment())+

                ggplot2::geom_histogram(fill="lightyellow",

alpha=.9,colour="grey60", size=.2) +

                ggplot2::geom_density(size=.2) +
                ggplot2::geom_vline(xintercept =
slope.0,color="red",linetype=2,size=.7)+
                ggplot2::xlab("Estimated slopes")+
                ggplot2::theme(axis.text = element_text(size=14),

(I also doubt setting the environment to environment() is the right
thing to do, but it's hard to know without more context)

Hadley

