Ser,

I get that the data represents week, although you don't indicate which ones, and I understand that you have a formula, but why does every row have a formula?

Usually you would plot one versus the other.

require(ggplot2)

ggplot(data = df, aes(x=World, y=France) +
geom_point()

If I had to take a guess, and I am not a statistician, it does not look like you need a fourth order polynomial to describe your data.

For the love of dog, please reply to the list.

B

