MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Dear all,

publication of figures often requires the labeling of panels/facets.
For this purpose I wrote a simple brittle function to do just that.

I'm not versed enough yet with ggplot to make the function aware of the
default data set of a ggplot  object, so i have the data fed in now.  It
works nicely for me with its defaults.  Hopefully it is helpful for you.

library(ggplot2)
label_facet <- function(facets, data, labels=paste0(LETTERS, ")"), x=-Inf,
                        y=Inf, hjust=-.2, vjust=1.4,
                        size=rel(3.6), fontface="bold", ...)
{
    d.f <- ddply(data, facets, length)
    d.f$labels <- labels[1:nrow(d.f)]
    geom_text(aes(label=labels), data=d.f, x=x, y=y,
              hjust=hjust, vjust=vjust, size=size, fontface=fontface, ...)
}

p <- ggplot(mpg, aes(x=factor(cyl), y=hwy)) + geom_boxplot()
p + facet_wrap( ~ class, nrow=2)+ label_facet(~class, mpg)
p + facet_grid(drv ~ year) + label_facet(drv ~ year, mpg)

Cheers,
Brian

