Quick update: via twitter Hadley suggested looking at coord_quickmap() <https://twitter.com/hadleywickham/status/636333323179024384>. I don't have a good explanation as to why, but this code:

library(choroplethr)
library(ggplot2)

data(df_pop_state)

state_choropleth(df_pop_state)
state_choropleth(df_pop_state) + coord_quickmap()

gives a projection without triggering the custom_annotation error that "+ coord_map()" does. I'm going to incorporate this into the next version of choroplethr.

