Haha, I'm not trying to do anything nefarious, I'm just trying to create an  "break" in the x axis, because I have an important data point at a really low x value (2 May 2011), and if I didn't create the break it would be a boring graph full of empty space between the early data point, and the data I want to plot which is in Aug-Oct 2015.  To do this, I've assigned the 2 May point a false x-value to bring it close, then manually edited the x-axis labels to make them accurate.  Then I added a vertical line to indicate the "break".

Actually, I just want to do what BreakXAxis does in Matlab:
http://www.mathworks.com/matlabcentral/fileexchange/3683-breakxaxis

and as far as I know ggplot can't do this (http://stackoverflow.com/questions/7194688/using-ggplot2-can-i-insert-a-break-in-the-axis)

Dennis, thanks, I think I understand what you are suggesting now and I'll try it.

